ve 8.\n\nAmong valid singles in my hand:\n- ♥10 (rank 10) > 8 → valid\n- ♣J (J) > 10 → better than needed\n- Similarly, ♥K, ♥A, ♦2 are overkill\n\nSo the most efficient play is **♥10** — it wins the trick without overcommitting.\n\nAlso, by playing a 10, I signal that I am not desperate (I can follow up), and I leave room for my teammate to potentially take control later with their own high cards.\n\nReason: Play the minimal winning card to conserve high-value cards for future critical moments. Since the landlord is not under heavy pressure yet, efficient card usage is key. Playing ♥10 beats ♦8 and preserves stronger cards like ♦2 for bombs or endgame control.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥10"]}'}
